1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:05,646
Meet Veroniqa, your AI assistant for API testing.

2
00:00:05,766 --> 00:00:10,086
She turns your requirements into tests that run, and results you can trust.

3
00:00:11,586 --> 00:00:19,048
Start a project, and give her what your team already has: requirement documents, PDF files, or links to your docs.

4
00:00:19,168 --> 00:00:24,010
Every source is indexed, and scanned for prompt injection before she ever reads it.

5
00:00:25,510 --> 00:00:27,538
Ask a question in plain English.

6
00:00:27,658 --> 00:00:32,239
Veroniqa answers from your own documents, and shows the passages she used.

7
00:00:32,359 --> 00:00:35,685
If the answer isn't there, she tells you, instead of guessing.

8
00:00:37,185 --> 00:00:38,747
Links are fetched safely.

9
00:00:38,867 --> 00:00:45,316
Internal and cloud-metadata addresses are refused, so your knowledge base can't be turned against your network.

10
00:00:46,816 --> 00:00:49,224
When you're ready, just say: run the tests.

11
00:00:49,344 --> 00:00:56,886
Veroniqa plans, writes and runs API tests against your service, then triages every failure, with evidence.

12
00:00:57,006 --> 00:01:01,550
In this demo, she found both planted bugs, with 46 tests passing.

13
00:01:03,050 --> 00:01:09,084
Behind her, the AgentQA engine gives easy work to cheaper models, and checks every result.

14
00:01:09,204 --> 00:01:16,294
On our simulated benchmark, it found 94% of the planted bugs, at 47% of the cost.

15
00:01:17,794 --> 00:01:21,154
Veroniqa. Ask, add knowledge, and run the tests.
